# Generated data tabulations, not source. They are rebuilt by the scripts named
# in their own headers (tools/fetch_photon_data.py, tools/convert_photon_data.py)
# and reviewing them line by line means reviewing a physics tabulation, which a
# diff cannot help with. Collapsing them keeps a data refresh from burying the
# code it comes with: the bremsstrahlung file alone is 28,520 lines.
#
# They stay uncompressed on purpose. `endf` is deliberately dependency-free,
# which is what lets its tables split out without dragging a parser into the
# wasm build, and reading these through xz would make a decompressor a real
# dependency rather than a dev-dependency. It would also cost time rather than
# save it: a full load is about 13 ms, and decompressing 2.4 MB of xz is more
# than that again. The .xz fixtures under crates/endf/fixtures are a different
# case, read only by tests through a dev-dependency.
packages/yamc-core/python/yamc/data/*.txt linguist-generated=true -diff
